# Token Architecture

Every visual value in osionos is a CSS custom property named `--osio-*`, and they
all live in **exactly one file**: `src/app/styles/global.css`. That file is the
single source of truth for colour, typography, spacing, radius, shadow, and motion.
Everything else in the app references it with `var(--osio-…)`.

> [!note] Why one file
> Colour values in one place means a re-skin is an edit to that file, not a sweep
> across the codebase. The file is deliberately the one large module the app's
> ≤200-line convention exempts.

## Token families

The names read as **semantic roles**, not raw colours — you reach for
`--osio-fg-default`, never "the dark grey".

| Family | Examples | Role |
|:-------|:---------|:-----|
| Background | `--osio-bg-page` · `--osio-bg-surface` · `--osio-bg-panel` · `--osio-bg-hover` | canvas & panels |
| Foreground | `--osio-fg-default` · `--osio-fg-strong` · `--osio-fg-muted` · `--osio-fg-inverse` | text ink |
| Border | `--osio-border-default` · `--osio-border-soft` · `--osio-border-strong` | hairlines |
| Accent | `--osio-accent` · `--osio-accent-hover` · `--osio-accent-text` · `--osio-accent-subtle` | brand terracotta |
| Status | `--osio-update` · `--osio-danger` · `--osio-success` · `--osio-warning` | intent colours |
| Block tints | `--osio-block-tint-blue-bg` … `-red` `-green` `-yellow` `-purple` `-brown` (bg + fg) | callout / highlight tints |
| Graph | `--osio-graph-bg-0/1` · `--osio-graph-ink` · `--osio-graph-edge-*` · `--osio-graph-select` | force-graph materials |
| Type | `--osio-font-family-sans/serif/mono` · `--osio-font-size-*` · `--osio-font-weight-*` | typography |
| Shape | `--osio-radius-*` · `--osio-shadow-*` · `--osio-border-width` | geometry |
| Motion | `--osio-motion-fast/standard/slow` · `--osio-ease-out` | animation |

## Rules the tokens follow

- [x] Colour tokens are **6-character hex** only — predictable, greppable, diffable.
- [x] The **only** alpha token is `--osio-overlay`, by design (scrims are the one place transparency is a role).
- [x] `color-mix(in srgb, var(--osio-…) …%, …)` is allowed — it *references* a token, so it isn't a raw literal.
- [x] Spacing uses a **4px grid** (`--osio-space-*`) — row gap, section gap, and friends all snap to it.

## SCSS aliases

Some component styles are SCSS. There, colour `$`-variables **alias** the tokens
rather than hold values:

```scss
$accent: var(--osio-accent);   // colour → always a token reference
$sidebar-width: 260px;         // pure layout dimension → a literal is fine
```

Colour `$`-vars point at `var(--osio-*)`; only dimension constants (widths,
breakpoints) are allowed to be literal pixels.

> [!tip] Renaming a token is a breaking change
> The framework-agnostic graph engine resolves `--osio-graph-*` at runtime, and
> the docs markengine leans on `--osio-*` too. Rename a token and you silently
> change graph colours — treat token names as a public contract.

